it seems that most victories come with a  price that's no different in the world  of anime for every major victory or  reason to celebrate behind it is usually  a painful decision that a character has  had to make when you think about it it's  the sacrifice and the journey that makes  seeing light at the end of the tunnel  all the more sweeter right on that note  today we're looking at some of the most  emotional sacrifices in anime  [Music]  [Applause]  starting off the list is elaine  sacrificed from the seven deadly sins at  tenth place  ban and elaine didn't start out as best  friends the bandits spent a good chunk  of his past seeking the fountain of  youth only to keep getting thwarted by  the fountain's guardian elaine the two  soon develop feelings for each other  though alas happy moments have to win  don't they a demon attacks the forest  and wounds both ban and elaine and  instead of taking water from the  fountain for herself elaine makes band  drink it granting him the immortality  that he sought this flashback would  surely linger in the hearts of people  who watched the seven deadly sins for a  long long time  [Music]  foreign  jonathan joestar's death from jojo's  bizarre adventure is at number nine on  the list  having believed that he'd put an end to  his nemesis dio jonathan joestar spends  his last moments in phantom blood a  happy and married man that happiness  doesn't last long though as he gets  attacked once more by a still alive deo  during his honeymoon using the last of  his strength he traps deo and allows his  family to escape as he succumbs to his  wounds jonathan goes out with a smile  having saved his family and forgiving  his worst enemy jonathan's legacy  carries on for the series but even if  the series were to end at this point  he'd already be remembered as an  honorable man who paid the ultimate  price for the rest of the joestar family  [Music]  oh  [Music]  [Applause]  for our seventh moment we have vegeta  blowing himself up in an attempt to take  down majin buu at the time of his  introduction vegeta was shown to be  ruthless and uncaring he didn't give a  damn about anything but strength all in  all you can see why his eventual  decision to sacrifice himself in the  busag is one of the most gripping  moments of that arc despite not caring  about bulma and trunks it's obvious that  the prince of saiyans is lying and that  he's already completed the character  development that prompts him to  sacrifice himself for the world vegeta  realizes the consequences of all his  previous actions and decides to blow  himself up going down in a literal blaze  of glory he makes the choice of dying  for the world in an act of personal  redemption  [Applause]  [Music]  [Music]  at number six it's rider's doom battle  against gilgamesh from fate zero if  there's a list of all-time fake anime  moments rider's battle against gilgamesh  would surely make him this fight has it  all glorious noble fantasms heartwarming  farewell speeches and gilgamesh finally  finding a worthy opponent most of all it  showcases the fire of determination  burning within ryder's soul in one  climactic battle even while finding  himself completely outmatched against  the king of heroes ryder charges on  taking everything that the gate of  babylon can toss at him his sheer will  pushes him on but he was finally put  down for good  yuri  at the fifth spot we have a sacrificing  his life for luffy being a storyline  revolving around saving luffy's brother  part of the climax of the marine foot  arc ends with a cloud of despair looming  over our heroes akainu gets the upper  hand on ace and moves to finish off  luffy it's then the ace steps in and  takes the blow for his brother one that  would ultimately kill him instead of  possibly living on full of regret ace  makes the decision to die in an act of  protecting luffy he doesn't die in a  lost battle against someone out of his  own league but on his own terms it could  feel unfair especially to one piece fans  but ace's death has a legacy in it that  it finally convinces luffy that he has  to keep getting stronger  [Music]  foreign  [Music]  foreign  irwin smith's sacrifice against the  beast titan ranks fourth on the list  while the commander of the survey corps  did care for his men he's ruthless and  wouldn't hesitate in sacrificing them  for the betterment of mankind needless  to say the command is someone who's  caused the deaths of hundreds of people  soon though he reflects on his actions  and realizes that he's been a hypocrite  all along he's unwilling to die for the  greater cause while preaching that  ideology to justify his orders and the  inner desire that's fueled by a moment  with his father it's this realization  that drives him to lead the charge  against the beast titan this distraction  gives levi the opening needed to  confront and defeat zeke and in the end  it's irwin's desire to die with the  fallen recruits that pushes levi to save  the lethally wounded armin instead  leaving him to die after a moment of  redemption  [Music]  foreign  [Music]  in the battle against pain  during his infiltration mission jiraiya  finds himself in the battle against  konam it turns out that he has his work  cut out not only does he have to contend  with konan he has to fight for his life  against pain or what's supposed to be  pain if then that he finds out that pain  is actually an entity composed of  multiple bodies armed with unique powers  despite his valiant efforts jariah finds  himself overwhelmed by the pains there's  hope at the end of the master ninja's  life he dies not with sadness or regrets  but with a smile  knowing that he's done his part in his  last moments he entrusts the world to  the pupil who he knows would soon carve  his spot in history as the savior of the  world  [Music]  sacrifice at the end of code geass takes  the second spot on the list  still held as one of the most iconic  endings to a legendary series it would  be hard to top lelouch's sacrifice at  the end of code gyas taking in the  hatred of the world and directing it  towards him as an all-powerful demagogue  lelouch finishes his longtime plan with  suzaku by having suzaku take the guys of  zero and kill him truly a gutsy plan at  the cost of the greatest sacrifice given  everything else has happened would  anything less have sufficed with the one  focus of hatred gone lelouch cements  himself as a messianic archetype one who  has paid the ultimate price to save the  world  [Music]  is  the number one sacrifice in anime  belongs to isaac naterro one of the most  defining and my personal favorite battle  in chimera ant arc is the one between  kimera and king marum and isaac notaro  chairman of the hunter association it's  a battle of two very powerful characters  at peak performance despite his withered  state and vulnerability after being  overpowered natero manages to strike  fear in meruem's heart claiming the  latter knows nothing about humanity's  endless potential for evolution and  malice nutero then pierces his own heart  with a finger and detonates the bomb in  a last attempt to put an end to  marowan's reign of terror for natero  that death is a satisfying one his long  search for a worthy opponent has finally  ended and he was able to pass away in  peace  [Music]  so what do you think then guys if you  have any suggestions on some moments  that we've missed do not hesitate to let  your voices be heard i'll see you next  time on vinicius  [Music]  yes  [Music]
 

